DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("2*(x/2)");
$fun_1 = Formula("6/((x^2+2*x+5))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("(((-infinity, 14))) U (0, 10)");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("((0, 10) - (-infinity, 14))");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-8, -4, 6, 7} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -8, -6, -4, 2, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-10, -8, -6, -4, 2, 6})");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("({-8, -4, 6, 7} U {-8, -4, 6, 7} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -4, 6, 7})) U {-10, -8, -6, -4, 2, 6} U {-8, -4, 6, 7}");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("({-10, -8, -6, -4, 2, 6}) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-8, -4, 6, 7}) U {-10, -8, -6, -4, 2, 6}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`9+9-7+9*2`]? [_____]{answer=>Real(29.),width=>3}
---

[`19/14+10`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('11.3571428571'),width=>10}
---

[`8+6+18*15`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('284'),width=>9}
---

[`7+3+17-13`] is equal to [_____]{14}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -8, -6, -4, 2, 6\}`]
- [`B = \{-8, -4, 6, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`B \cap A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(B \cup B \cap B) \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`(A) \cap B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x < 14\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 0 < x < 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`((A)) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`B - A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -7, -9, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 9, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 0, -10, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, -9, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<0, -10, -8>") x Compute("<-2, 9, 2>")}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, -9, -5>") x Compute("<-2, 9, 2>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, 9, 2>") x Compute("<-7, -9, -5>")}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, -7, 3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 8, 2, 5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<8, 2, 5>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, -7, 3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -7, 3>") . Compute("<8, 2, 5>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, 5>") . Compute("<-2, -7, 3>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, 5>") x Compute("<-2, -7, 3>")}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(4) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>4)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
